WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.290 --> 00:00:01.640
- People have been sending me tweets

00:00:01.640 --> 00:00:03.890
from @BadLegalTakes for a while,

00:00:03.890 --> 00:00:05.940
and I've really been enjoying them.

00:00:05.940 --> 00:00:07.730
And one of the ones that got my attention

00:00:07.730 --> 00:00:11.147
was originally a tweet
from PragerU who asks,

00:00:11.147 --> 00:00:12.950
"Is the death penalty ever moral?"

00:00:12.950 --> 00:00:15.130
And I'm sure PragerU has
an opinion on the subject,

00:00:15.130 --> 00:00:17.380
but the thing that got the
most attention was the reply

00:00:17.380 --> 00:00:18.827
from Redheaded Mermaid who tweeted,

00:00:18.827 --> 00:00:20.130
"No one gets the death penalty

00:00:20.130 --> 00:00:22.370
that didn't agree to it
with their attorney present.

00:00:22.370 --> 00:00:24.057
You watch too many movies."

00:00:25.530 --> 00:00:29.520
- I don't know where she
could have gotten this idea.

00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:31.710
I suppose that we all
agreed to the legal system

00:00:31.710 --> 00:00:33.380
through the social
contract, but it's kind of

00:00:33.380 --> 00:00:34.970
a philosophical fiction.

00:00:34.970 --> 00:00:36.815
Yeah, I mean you're
convicted involuntarily,

00:00:36.815 --> 00:00:39.080
you're then sentenced involuntarily.

00:00:39.080 --> 00:00:42.040
No one really agrees to the death penalty.

00:00:42.040 --> 00:00:44.050
I mean, there have been
a handful of situations

00:00:44.050 --> 00:00:46.780
where people have refused a pardon

00:00:46.780 --> 00:00:49.970
or requested the death
penalty for political reasons,

00:00:49.970 --> 00:00:51.510
but those are the
exceptions, not the rule.

00:00:51.510 --> 00:00:54.680
No one else really agrees
to the death penalty.

00:00:54.680 --> 00:00:55.513
Now you know!

